.TH MSYNC 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
msync \- synchronize a mapped range
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/mman.h>
.B int msync(void* address, size_t byte_count, int flags);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Synchronizes changes in a mapped range with its backing file. The address must
be page aligned. Flags include MS_SYNC, MS_ASYNC and MS_INVALIDATE.
See Linux msync(2) for the kernel's synchronization guarantees.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns zero, or \-1 with errno set. Success leaves errno unchanged.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mmap (3crunch),
.BR msync (2)
